Content: the machine's own PASSPROF / COMM-STOPFAST / CFGRETRY back onto main plus W906_QTCT (MinGW.org 6.3 has no QueryThreadCycleTime declaration -> resolved from kernel32 at run time); Jerry J-17 A (unsupported IO_CARD_TYPE -> loud diagnostic only: JsonBridge/CardTypeDiag.h, ChanIoPoints.cpp, ChanMotorPoints.cpp); St02 P1b (the RS-232 operator panel reads per chunk as golden: PadInterface_St02.cpp); Ifor01 POOL-2 (forms/fLotInfo.cpp, 3 #if 0 opened as golden 0618, 8 kept).
OLD 9 (all scanned for machine-only identifiers: 0 missing; NIGHT_REPORT.md drops one prose mention of W906_HT9050_AS_LS), NEW 3, WebMotorAccessLive.cpp / csystem.cpp merged = the machine's, tests/CMakeLists +2 tests (no duplicate registration).
Six conflicts, one by one: tools/wb_serve.cpp:239 (the PASSPROF line) and the PassProfEnd call take the laptop side -- it is the machine's line plus W906_QTCT, verified character for character after substituting the call back; wb_serve.cpp:4687 (the machine's IOTUNE cache-on-due) and EtherCAT/Pci1203Monitor.cpp:123 (the IO thread's ioPub / ioStaged) keep the machine side; the laptop's W906_ExitWatchdog* functions and PASSPROF banner already exist on the machine (:8881, :9337), so they are not added again; the last hunk differs only in the final newline. Resolved wb_serve differs from the machine's by 3 lines; definition counts unchanged. 3 files back to the machine's CRLF.

o2 full build 0 errors; ctest 387/404 (failures = the known list); production_audit first overlapped EastSun's F5 (18:11); after it closed: re-snapshot, the 27 package-related tests (25 pass; IoPoints / MotorPoints_HT9050 are on the known list), audit passes. Debug wb_serve 18:11 (EastSun's F5 build, includes this package), release 18:31. WORKLOG section 3 rows 161 and designer tools 0166 / 0167; the pending-items row updated for the evening.

